Changes
=======

v4.1.0 21 August 2026
  * Fix `--fix` pinning `go.mod` to a jwx version too old for the advice it
    gives. It wrote v4.0.0 while `jwk-parse-retains-unsupported-keys` told
    you to call `jwk.WithStrictKeySetParsing` and `jwk.IsUnsupportedKey`,
    which first shipped in v4.2.0, so the result did not compile. The version
    written is now the highest any rule that actually fired requires.
  * Report when `go.mod` is older than a reported rule needs, even where
    nothing else is left to migrate. These findings name the module, the
    version required, and the version you have, and exit 1 like any other
    remaining item. `--fix` raises the requirement for you.
  * Add ML-DSA rules for Go 1.27. A project whose `go.mod` declares go 1.27
    or later, using jwx v4.4.0 or later, no longer needs
    `github.com/jwx-go/mldsa/v4`: `--fix` drops that import and its
    requirement, moves `MLDSA44`/`MLDSA65`/`MLDSA87` calls to `jwa`, and
    swaps `filippo.io/mldsa` for `crypto/mldsa`. Below go 1.27 the rules stay
    silent, because none of it can be done there.
  * An import is never deleted while something still references it that
    cannot be rewritten, so `--fix` does not turn a building project into a
    broken one.
  * Rule schema version 3. Rules may declare `requires` (a `go` directive
    floor and module version floors), `package_import`, and `absorbed_into`;
    rule sets declare `minimum_target_version`. Existing rules are unaffected.

v4.0.4 24 July 2026
  * Add `jwk-parse-retains-unsupported-keys`, which reports v3 `jwk.Parse`
    calls whose JWK Set behavior changes in v4. v3 fails when an entry cannot
    be parsed; v4 retains it as a `jwk.UnsupportedKey` by default.

v4.0.3 7 May 2026
  * Add four missing v3→v4 rules for behavioral changes that
    `Changes-v4.md` documents but the migration tool wasn't
    surfacing: `jws-sign-kid-mismatch` (kid conflict between
    `WithKey` and `WithProtectedHeaders` is now an error in v4),
    `jws-verifycompactfast-strict-base64` (strict base64url in v4),
    `jwe-pbes2-defaults-raised` (10k → 600k/210k iteration count
    default), and `unregister-returns-error` (nine `Unregister*`
    functions across `jwk`/`jws`/`jwe`/`jwt`/`openid` changed from
    void to error-returning).
  * `settings-returns-error` rule now matches `jwk.Settings(...)`
    too; previously only `jwt`/`jws`/`jwe`/`cert.Settings` were
    patterned.

v4.0.2 28 Apr 2026
  * Accept `go`-style `./...` target patterns on the command line.
  * Show the matching source line inline in finding diagnostics.
  * Scan files that already import v4 (instead of skipping them) so
    leftover v3 calls in mixed-import files are reported.
  * Fix false-positive on bare `jwt.Parse` (no leading package import).
  * Fix-pass robustness: report `go mod tidy` failures, preserve
    original file modes, follow symlinks correctly, and propagate
    cancellation in delete contexts.

v4.0.1 19 Apr 2026
  * Auto-fix jwk.Import / jwk.Export / jwk.FromRaw call sites.
  * Auto-fix obj.Get(name, &dst) -> dst, err := pkg.Get[T](obj, name).
  * Rewrite github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v3 -> v4 in go.mod on -fix, then run
    `go mod tidy`.
  * Major scanner speedup on large consumers via narrowed packages.Load,
    per-module parallelism, and a per-batch typed-parse cache.

v4.0.0 19 Apr 2026
  * Initial release. Migration tool and machine-readable rules for moving
    code from github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v3 (and v2) to v4.
